    "narrative": "The Austin Waves project significant offensive upside today, spearheaded by **Kyle Tucker** (76.70) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), who headline our lineup with elite efficiency scores. **Kyle Tucker** faces a favorable matchup against JP Sears, where the weak xERA of 5.11 and the absence of a platoon penalty create an ideal environment for him to anchor the middle of the order. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our most efficient play against the Chandler matchup; his score is heavily buoyed by an excellent +14% platoon adjustment and an advantageous #2 spot in the lineup, making him a prime candidate to capitalize on RBI opportunities generated by the top of our order. **Gunnar Henderson** (70.61) remains a high-floor play despite a negative platoon swing against Lodolo, as his power profile and the leadoff position provide enough volume to sustain his value.\n\nStrategic park and platoon factors are driving our selection of **Cole Carrigg** (69.36) and **Heliot Ramos** (61.74). **Cole Carrigg** benefits from a massive +14% park factor adjustment, while **Heliot Ramos** leverages a similar venue boost alongside a \"Slow SP Delivery\" indicator, which increases our stolen base probability\u2014a critical consideration given our strategy to overweight speed. The most difficult bench decision involved **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.13). While his raw talent is undeniable, a -5% park penalty and a unfavorable matchup against the efficiency of Emerson Hancock dropped him just below the threshold required to displace starters like **Coby Mayo** (66.71). \n\nManagement is monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, most notably for **Liam Hicks** (43.01) and **Nasim Nunez** (60.85). While **Nasim Nunez** earns a strong start based on the favorable xERA of the opposing pitcher, his floor is sensitive to his projected #9 spot. We are also wary of the base stealing threat posed by **Andy Pages** (71.11) facing an elite hold pitcher, which slightly dampens his aggressive upside. All rostered players should be monitored for late-afternoon weather shifts, though as of now, the primary risk remains the potential for lower-order lineup shifts for our pending starters.",
